course: dictionary
lesson: 9556
title: Stormy: weather and feelings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Stormy describes weather with strong winds, heavy rain, thunder or big waves. «The little boat was tossed about on the stormy sea.» The word stormy tells you the sea was rough and dangerous, not calm.
explain: Stormy can also describe feelings or meetings full of anger and shouting. «They had a stormy argument about the football match.» Here stormy has nothing to do with the weather. It means loud and angry.
explain: Use the words around stormy to choose its meaning. If the sentence mentions waves, wind, thunder or lightning, it is about weather. If it mentions shouting, slammed doors or angry voices, it is about feelings. Then swap in your meaning and check that it makes sense.
fact: Stormy means full of strong winds, heavy rain, thunder or big waves, or full of anger and shouting.
fact: Stormy is an adjective, and it changes to stormier and stormiest when you compare things.
fact: «A dark and stormy night» is a cliché: a phrase used so often that it has lost its power.
fact: In French, a dreadful stormy day is «un temps de chien», which means "a dog's weather".
fact: Mary Anning, a girl from a poor family in Lyme Regis, England, hunted for fossils along stormy cliffs and beaches.
exercise: «The stormy sea tossed the little boat.» What does stormy describe here? | Calm, still water with no wind | A sea that is warm and sunny | * Rough weather with big waves | A sea full of fish
exercise: «They had a stormy argument, full of shouting.» What does stormy mean in this sentence? | A quiet picnic in the park | A rainy walk to school | * A loud, angry argument | A warm and sunny meeting
exercise: Stormy comes from a word you already know. Which word is it? | star | story | * storm | stir
test: «Stay indoors and keep away from the beach in stormy weather.» Why is this good advice? | * Big waves and strong winds can be dangerous | The beach is closed for painting | Indoors is always cold | Stormy weather is good for swimming
test: Which word is the comparative form of stormy, as in "the wind is ___ today than yesterday"? | * Stormier | Stormly | Stormiest | More stormy
exam: Which sentence uses stormy to mean full of anger and shouting? | The stormy sky lit up with lightning | The stormy beach was empty and quiet | The stormy waves crashed on the rocks | * Their stormy meeting ended with shouting and slammed doors
